ering\nEnvironmental Science\nFood Science\nMechanical and Production Engineering\nQuantitative Genetics and Genomics\nCivil and Architectural Engineering\nThe Civil and Architectural PhD programme hosts approx. 20 PhD students. Focus is on applied research and we enjoy strong collaboration with the industry on core issues in all of our research areas.\nMeet our PhD students\nResearch facilities\nWithin the department, advanced laboratory facilities are available. Graduate students are expected to take part in developing novel equipment.\nCollaboration with the industry also ensures access to state-of-the-art industrial R&D facilities.\nGeographic location\nThe localisation strategy of the department aims to ensure that the educations and research activities are placed in the scientific environment to which they are most closely related.\nThe academic environment help strengthen the growing cluster of technology are centered in Aarhus and ensure continued positive commercial development in the region.\nEmployment after graduation\nMost engineering graduates take up a career in the industry or in consultancy; both are areas where project leadership is important, and this often becomes a stepping stone towards leadership.\nHead of Programme\nMassimo Fiorentini\nAssociate Professor\nM massimo@cae.au.dk\nH 3210 Navitas, 04.103\nP +4593522961\nLocal Programme Secretary\nMalene Kjerulf Christensen\nChief/Special Consultant\nM mkc@cae.au.dk\nH 3210 Navitas, 03.075\nP +4520814286\nGSTS PhD Partner\nWinni Siig Nielsen\nPhD Partner\nM winni.siig@au.dk\nH 1521 - 128\nP +4593522834\nP +4593522834\nMore information for enrolled PhD students at our employee portal\nRevised\n07.05.2026\n-\ncae@au.dk\nGraduate School of Technical Sciences\nNy Munkegade 120, building 1521\n8000 Aarhus C.\nSee location on a map\nCVR-nr: 31119103\nEAN-nr: 57 98 000 433 779\nAbout us\nAbout GSTS\nContact\nDegree programmes\nBachelor\nMaster\nPhD\n\u00a9 \u2014\nCookies at au.dk\nPrivacy policy\nWeb Acc